# Spheres, Meme Computers and Symbolic Systems
=> index.gmi Return to the research manuscript
=> references.gmi Sources

## Diagram terminology
Patasphere: proposed outer interpretive layer, possibly connected to 'pataphysics; its intended definition remains open.
Infosphere: information and records.
Semiosphere: cultural systems of signs and signification (Yuri Lotman).
Noosphere: planetary human thought and knowledge (Vernadsky; Teilhard de Chardin).
Logosphere: language, reason, discourse and logos (usage varies).
Cybersphere: networked digital technologies and computation.
Simulacrosphere: models, simulations and representations (proposed label).

These are overlapping conceptual domains, not scientifically established concentric physical shells. The noosphere and cybersphere can intersect.

## Meme computers
A proposed analytic term for distributed systems in which symbols, beliefs, interpretations, institutions, people and machines form information-processing feedback loops with real consequences.
Example: ecological observations -> Rachel Carson's Silent Spring -> public interpretation -> collective mobilization -> policy -> new environmental observations.
A process can transform the world without being conscious or a unified intentional agent.

## Comparative poles
Land: acceleration and technocapital feedback.
VALIS: fictional revelation and possible corrective intelligence.
Logopolis: fictional cosmic maintenance through collective computation.
Deep Thought and Earth: computation, question formation and planetary scale.
Roko's Basilisk: hypothetical anticipatory incentives, not proven retrocausality.
Silent Spring: empirically traceable ecological feedback and correction.

## Epistemic labels
OBSERVED — documented historical/physical process.
INTERPRETIVE — philosophical model or analogy.
FICTIONAL — narrative events and entities.
SPECULATIVE — unverified possibility or extrapolation.
